{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1781614275,"nonce":"qiS33hwCUXWYVSlkAJLr42RxSe8=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABFpx9Ug","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/285","origin":"github"},"title":"Lake Massabesic datum: move to polygon config (datum_config_path), drop scalar lake_datum","message":"## Make the polygon datum config the live source for Lake Massabesic\n\nThe `chart_datum` node (mru_transform) already supports polygon→datum config via `datum_config_path` (precedence: `lake_datum` param \u003e `override:true` polygon \u003e VDatum). Move BizzyBoat from the scalar `lake_datum` param to a polygon entry so it's the single source of truth (toward UMA #163, shared with the bathy store importer).\n\n### Plan (option A — polygon live)\n1. **Add** `bizzyboat_project11/config/massabesic_datum_polygons.yaml`:\n   - `name: \"Lake Massabesic\"`, `override: true`, **`chart_datum_z: 48.88`** (full-pool WGS84 ellipsoidal — derivation in #278), `mhhw_z` omitted (no tide; keeps `map_tide` unfiltered per #278).\n   - `ring`: the contour-raster (`massabesic_bathy.tif`, NAD83/UTM19N) lat/lon extent padded ~0.5 km — covers the lake + buffer.\n2. **Wire** `datum_config_path` in `core_launch.py` via `FindPackageShare('bizzyboat_project11')/config/...` (package-relative).\n3. **Remove** the scalar `lake_datum: 48.88` from `bizzyboat.yaml` so the polygon drives `chart_datum`.\n\n### Trade-off accepted\nWith the scalar gone, `chart_datum` publishes only when the boat is inside the (padded) ring — fine on the lake; would drop during transport/wild-fix. Accepted for the single-source-of-truth design.\n\nPart of rolker/unh_marine_autonomy#163. Datum value from #278.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}